					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-10912288#post-4204723</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-10912288/bearitage-collection#post-4204723</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Apr 2019 20:35:26 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Genshed</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2643500</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I actually had a dream about being stalked by a bear this morning, so this was well timed.</p> <p>Fun fact: the term 'bear', from a word meaning 'brown', was used to refer to the animal named 'arkto' in Proto-Indo-European, because using its proper name was believed to summon it. Different European languages developed a variety of euphemisms for 'the brown one', such as 'bee-wolf', from which the hero Beowulf derived his name.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
